events.content:
Build succeeds — the `after` callback fired during static generation as expected (per the docs: since the page has no dynamic APIs, it's prerendered and `after` runs at build time).

**`app/page.tsx`**
```tsx
import { after } from 'next/server'
import { logPageView } from '@/app/analytics'

export default function Home() {
  after(() => {
    logPageView('home')
  })

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Welcome</h1>
    </main>
  )
}
```

**`app/analytics.ts`** — a stub `logPageView` service call.

This follows the `after` API documented in this fork's local docs (`node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/04-functions/after.md`), imported from `next/server`, which schedules the analytics call to run after the response is sent without blocking it. Verified with `tsc --noEmit` and `next build`.

